# Workflow Reference

## Source Of Truth

```
$OPENCTO_WORKSPACE/workflows/{workflow_id}/    <- Git-backed source, committed
$OPENCTO_WORKSPACE/workflows/{workflow_id}/data/  <- persistent runtime data, Git-ignored
```

Runtime snapshots, logs, caches, dependency folders, and build outputs are not source of truth.

## Directory Layout

```
$OPENCTO_WORKSPACE/
  workflows/
    {workflow_id}/
      workflow.yml          <- editable manifest
      src/                  <- default location for implementation files
      data/                 <- persistent cross-run data, Git-ignored
      .git/                 <- do not edit directly
      .gitignore            <- managed by OpenCTO; append custom ignores at the bottom only
  workflow-runs/
    {workflow_id}/
      {run_id}/
        workflow.yml
        src/
        artifacts/          <- step outputs shared within this run
```

`src/` is the default location for implementation files, but workflow source is not limited to `src/`. Scripts, configs, and packages may live anywhere in the workflow directory unless the path is reserved or ignored.

`workflow-runs/{workflow_id}/{run_id}/` is a per-run snapshot. Runtime evidence only — never edit it.

### Managed, Reserved, and Ignored Paths

`workflow.yml` is the manifest and must be edited when authoring the workflow. `.gitignore` is managed by OpenCTO; append custom ignores only when necessary.

Do not edit or write source files under the runtime data directory, Git internals, or generated/ignored output paths. Ignored directory names are rejected at any depth (e.g. `src/node_modules/` is rejected).

```
.git/, data/,
output/, tmp/, temp/, .cache/,
node_modules/, dist/, build/, target/,
venv/, .venv/, __pycache__/, .pytest_cache/,
.DS_Store, *.log
```

## Runtime Environment Variables

Set by OpenCTO at step execution time. Do not hardcode their values.

```
OPENCTO_WORKFLOWS_DIR     — root of all workflow source repos under $OPENCTO_WORKSPACE.
                            Each workflow lives at OPENCTO_WORKFLOWS_DIR/{workflow_id}/.
                            Read-only during step execution.
OPENCTO_WORKFLOW_DATA_DIR — persistent data directory at OPENCTO_WORKFLOWS_DIR/{workflow_id}/data/.
                            Git-ignored and writable at step runtime.
                            Use for state or outputs future scheduled runs must read.
OPENCTO_WORKFLOW_RUN_DIR  — current run snapshot directory and step working directory.
                            Runtime evidence only. Not available to future runs.
OPENCTO_WORKFLOW_RUN_ARTIFACTS_DIR
                          — writable same-run artifact directory for files that later steps
                            in the same run should read. Not available to future runs.

```

